The attached image, Fig. 6 in the provided context, illustrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles enhance the expression of costimulatory molecules on dendritic cells (DCs). Flow cytometry histograms show that bone marrow-derived DCs incubated with 250 µg/mL Nano-11 (black line) for two days exhibit a marked increase in CD80 and CD86 expression compared to medium control cells (gray line). CD40 expression shows only a slight increase. This indicates that Nano-11 activates DCs, promoting the expression of crucial costimulatory molecules necessary for initiating an adaptive immune response.